Posting a follow up question in case others have similar questions:

"If I have donor 1-5 across 2 conditions (each donor have two conditions), should I use "D1" instead of "C1D1", correct?"

My response: Here, I would use "D1" instead of "C1D1".  Supplementary table 3 & supplementary figure 6 should be good references (link <https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpubs.acs.org%2Fdoi%2Fsuppl%2F10.1021%2Facs.jproteome.2c00834%2Fsuppl_file%2Fpr2c00834_si_001.pdf&data=05%...%40northeastern.edu%7Cf76e6f94909443d8efe808dde1e93ac3%7Ca8eec281aaa34daeac9b9a398b9215e7%7C0%7C0%7C638915114207826190%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=VejEDd7yVTxcUUJf6tTXyfE9y%2BbS6k7ka1zL8H0ihCQ%3D&reserved=0>).  This study can be treated like a paired design.

